update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Cloud Crush, a girls hockey co-op of St. Cloud Apollo, Tech and Cathedral students, host the Academy of Holy Angels in MSHSL varsity play at the MAC. The Crush program has been around more than 25 years, and in February 2026 it became the first St. Cloud girls team to reach the state tournament.$about$ where id = '0e7e8c11-614d-4839-8d3e-ea5929ea35b9';  -- St. Cloud Girls Hockey vs Academy of Holy Angels
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Bennies host league-leading Carleton in their last home match of the regular season, an NCAA Division III MIAC game at CSB's Outdoor Athletic Complex. Saint Benedict comes in 11-1-2 (6-1-2 MIAC), and Carleton is unbeaten in league play at 9-0. First-year Eva Gower leads CSB with 10 goals, and senior keeper Rhianna Anya leads the MIAC in save percentage. The match also streams on the MIAC Sports Network.$about$ where id = 'cf006d38-9582-4212-91c3-0ac00b32a034';  -- CSB Soccer vs Carleton
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict volleyball hosts Augsburg in an NCAA Division III MIAC match that doubles as CSB's All Cancer Awareness/Dig Pink game, raising money for the Coborn's Cancer Center. The Bennies are 11-9 (5-2 MIAC) after a Friday win at St. Olaf, and they lead the all-time series with Augsburg 48-10. Tickets are sold online through CSB+SJU, card only, no cash.$about$ where id = '2ce82280-4b1f-46f6-a364-978cde9952f0';  -- CSB Volleyball vs Augsburg
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict swim and dive opens its home season with a dual meet against MIAC rival Macalester. The Bennies started the year sixth of nine teams at the MIAC vs. WIAC meet in Rochester. CSB swims its home meets at Warner Palaestra Pool on the Saint John's campus, and Saint John's hosts Macalester's men the same day.$about$ where id = '62de53e5-6342-42da-a6ff-6e9d3036dc40';  -- CSB Swim and Dive vs Macalester
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict volleyball hosts Augsburg in an NCAA Division III MIAC match that doubles as CSB's All Cancer Awareness/Dig Pink game, raising money for the Coborn's Cancer Center. The Bennies are 11-9 (5-2 MIAC) after a Friday win at St. Olaf, and they lead the all-time series with Augsburg 48-10. Tickets are sold online through CSB+SJU, card only, no cash.$about$ where id = '122af3e7-d164-403c-9f2b-145b49bf0a32';  -- CSB Volleyball vs Augsburg
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict opens its 2026-27 women's basketball season at home against Minnesota-Morris, the night's second game of CSB's Tipoff Tournament. The Bennies play NCAA Division III ball in the MIAC under head coach Mike Durbin and went 16-9 (11-7 MIAC) last season. CSB beat Morris 91-57 a year ago. One ticket covers both of the night's tournament games, 6:15 and 8:15 p.m.$about$ where id = 'e16d29b9-d8c6-4789-a17c-d8576baaa8fe';  -- CSB Basketball vs Minnesota-Morris
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Fall Finale is CSB cross country's last home race of the season, a 5,000-meter meet in Collegeville. It comes the week after the MIAC Championships and before the NCAA Division III North Region meet. Last year Abby Bufkin won the individual title and the Bennies took the team title.$about$ where id = '3f3aa33f-3d19-438b-ae1d-2214e245aab7';  -- CSB Cross Country vs Fall Finale
update public.club_events set description = $about$Day two of CSB's Tipoff Tournament brings Loras to Claire Lynch Hall. The Bennies play NCAA Division III women's basketball in the MIAC under head coach Mike Durbin and went 16-9 (11-7 MIAC) last season. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = '6aeddbc1-c9b2-4173-811c-68257cb8b8c2';  -- CSB Basketball vs Loras
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict volleyball closes its regular season at home against Carleton in an NCAA Division III MIAC match. The MIAC playoffs start the following Tuesday, hosted by the higher seed. CSB swept Carleton in last year's meeting. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = '845fbfb4-0eef-4f15-b01a-9de5f2bbc0ea';  -- CSB Volleyball vs Carleton
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict women's basketball hosts Central (Iowa) in the MN v Iowa Clash, a nonconference weekend at Claire Lynch Hall. The Bennies play NCAA Division III ball in the MIAC under head coach Mike Durbin and went 16-9 last season. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = 'b87272ff-4aa1-4981-8b74-62b702aa7cde';  -- CSB Basketball vs Central
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict women's basketball closes the MN v Iowa Clash weekend against Simpson, from Iowa. It is CSB's last home game before MIAC play opens in December. The Bennies play NCAA Division III ball under head coach Mike Durbin and went 16-9 last season.$about$ where id = '2a39bfe7-fe60-4fd4-8a31-7814c2ff4e04';  -- CSB Basketball vs Simpson
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Olaf visits for Saint Benedict's first MIAC home game of the 2026-27 women's basketball season. The Bennies, coached by Mike Durbin, went 11-7 in the NCAA Division III MIAC last season. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = 'cfa2cff5-c6ea-43f9-9ca9-a1688135022d';  -- CSB Basketball vs St. Olaf
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict women's basketball hosts Augsburg in an NCAA Division III MIAC game, a weeknight matchup at Claire Lynch Hall. The Bennies, coached by Mike Durbin, went 16-9 (11-7 MIAC) last season. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = '3cbb7c79-5115-4861-bac1-2b1a5435d932';  -- CSB Basketball vs Augsburg
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Benedict women's basketball hosts Bethel in an NCAA Division III MIAC game on Alumnae Day, when former Bennies come back to Claire Lynch Hall. CSB, coached by Mike Durbin, went 16-9 (11-7 MIAC) last season. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = '909fe00b-3ef9-4bfe-a07c-fb48d49ca55f';  -- CSB Basketball vs Bethel: Alumnae Day
update public.club_events set description = $about$Gustavus Adolphus visits Claire Lynch Hall for a midweek NCAA Division III MIAC women's basketball game. Saint Benedict, coached by Mike Durbin, went 16-9 (11-7 MIAC) last season. Tickets are sold through CSB+SJU ticketing, card only.$about$ where id = '4d926a7d-222c-4b67-b4b9-1284e18168f8';  -- CSB Basketball vs Gustavus Adolphus
update public.club_events set description = $about$The CSB+SJU Vocal Performance Workshop stages Once Upon a Stage, a fully produced show of scenes from musical theater and opera. Student singers perform songs from Beauty and the Beast, Cinderella, The Marriage of Figaro, Little Women, Hansel and Gretel and Into the Woods. Tickets are $7 for adults, seniors and faculty/staff and $3 for students, through tickets.csbsju.edu.$about$ where id = '52962997-4cf3-4654-bf56-a546128f860e';  -- Vocal Performance Workshop
update public.club_events set description = $about$Bréagán is a joint exhibit by Chloe Briggs and Liam J. McLaughlin about lineage, family stories and the truths and falsehoods that shape who we are. Briggs, mainly an oil painter, looks at Midwestern family memory through stories and photographs; McLaughlin's video and wall works weave myth, history and immigrant identity. The opening reception runs 5 to 7 p.m., and the show stays up through Dec. 17.$about$ where id = '59a314d3-73a7-4e73-a911-aa4ff613b76f';  -- "Bréagán" opening reception
update public.club_events set description = $about$Minnesota pianist Lorie Line brings her Christmas tour to Saint John's, playing holiday favorites, telling stories and taking song requests on the spot, including her known mashup medleys. It is a solo piano show of about 90 minutes with no intermission, for ages 10 and up. Tickets are $79, fees included.$about$ where id = 'f0691d93-f83c-40f2-b895-5bddf08594ac';  -- Christmas with Lorie Line
update public.club_events set description = $about$Christmas with Saint Ben's & Saint John's is the colleges' decades-old holiday tradition of music and readings, with nearly 150 student musicians from the Chamber Choir, Men's Chorus, Women's Choir, Orchestra and Brass Choir. The program mixes carols, spoken word and choral works, including Hovland's The Glory of the Father. The St. John's Boys' Choir joins the Great Hall shows. Tickets are $22 for adults, $20 for seniors 60+ and $15 for students.$about$ where id = '4780b81d-aa6f-4770-85db-717ed0da00c7';  -- Christmas with CSB SJU
update public.club_events set description = $about$Students put on a night of live music at Brother Willie's Pub, with the bar open for those 21 and over. Swayed Pines is an old CSB+SJU name: a folk festival students ran from 1974 to 2000, brought back as a student variety show in 2022.$about$ where id = 'd0a11e35-9309-4011-a785-c6ebbcdcaa4d';  -- Swayed Pines!
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint Ben's Campus Ministry leads a weekly Holy Hour of Eucharistic Adoration, quiet prayer before the Blessed Sacrament. It meets Wednesdays in Regina Chapel, on the lower level of Regina Hall in Mary Commons, and is open to all.$about$ where id = '832fefef-20f1-4550-acaf-d1179caf61c3';  -- Adoration: Saint Ben's Campus Ministry
