update public.club_events set description = $about$The Banff Mountain Film Festival World Tour stops at Saint John's for an evening of about 10 short adventure films on sports, cultures, people and places, picked from the yearly festival in Banff, Alberta. Doors open at 6:30 p.m. in Pellegrene Auditorium. Community tickets are $14 for Outdoor U members and $20 for others, and each CSB+SJU student gets one free ticket. Ticket sales fund Collegebound, an outdoor program for first-year students.$about$ where id = '8459be74-684b-4758-a758-480c679e187e';  -- Banff Mountain Film Festival
update public.club_events set description = $about$A two-hour Outdoor U walk through the Saint John's Abbey Arboretum to find and identify the tracks animals leave in winter snow. It is free for Outdoor U members and CSB+SJU students; nonmembers pay $10, with a $20 cap per family. Registration is through Outdoor U's online store.$about$ where id = 'a5594faf-2e09-44c6-ad6a-60beeffc8621';  -- Animal tracking at Outdoor U
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Minnesota Master Naturalist volunteer course, Big Woods, Big Rivers, runs as a week-long, 40-hour class at Saint John's, Feb. 1 to 5, 8 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. each day. It covers the biome in winter and trains people to volunteer as naturalists. The course costs $295, with scholarships available through the Minnesota Master Naturalist Program. Registration had not opened yet when checked.$about$ where id = '7b0a4f92-6ac8-4a58-b3d8-cd873e767f56';  -- MN Master Naturalist
update public.club_events set description = $about$Outdoor U's Luminary Hikes light a path across Lake Sagatagan to the Stella Maris Chapel on two winter nights, Feb. 12 and 13. The walk starts and ends at the Lake Sagatagan beach, reached by the path between the Abbey Guesthouse and the Abbey Church; the closest parking is the church lots. It is free and open to all with no registration, and donations to Outdoor U are welcome.$about$ where id = '44cf04c5-4845-46ed-bacb-58771e4dccf7';  -- Luminary Hikes at the Abbey Arboretum
update public.club_events set description = $about$A backyard ultra on the Lake Wobegon Trail, organized by Sartell graduate Gavin Buersken. Runners finish a 4.167-mile loop within each hour, and a new loop starts at the top of every hour until one runner is left. It starts at 8 a.m. from the Lake Wobegon Visitor Center in St. Joseph, with sign-up from 7 a.m. or by the QR code in the City's post. Entry is free, and local businesses donated prizes for a raffle during the race.$about$ where id = '2abd82ff-ede5-403b-b8b3-cea25e60dc42';  -- Wobegon Trail Backyard Ultra
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph's adult Halloween dodgeball tournament returns to the Kennedy Community School gym. Teams of up to eight play a double-elimination bracket, with prizes for first and second place and a prize for best costume, so dressing up is part of the fun.$about$ where id = '3eb10cc4-6df2-4187-9563-b81e587fb859';  -- Adult Halloween Dodgeball Tournament
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph Parks and Rec hosts a morning of Halloween crafts in the Centennial Park shelter for kids ages 2 to 14. It costs $5 per child, and costumes are welcome.$about$ where id = 'e48c28ad-c4c3-463b-af74-a40717e2829e';  -- Fall Craft Day
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council, Mayor Adam Scepaniak and four councilmembers, meets in a work session the hour before its regular meeting. The council's meetings are open to the public. Agendas and minutes are in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '46334f92-8eb5-4700-8c55-d8fb1d993e49';  -- City Council Work Session
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council, Mayor Adam Scepaniak and four councilmembers, meets the first and third Monday of each month at the Government Center to pass ordinances, set city policy and manage the budget. Meetings are open to the public and air live on the local cable channel. Agendas and minutes are in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '1fa3240a-1789-449e-8511-1bab8b2386ef';  -- City Council Meeting
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph Parks and Rec runs a four-session youth basketball program for grades 3 to 5 in the Kennedy Community School gym. A past session of the same program taught shooting, dribbling, passing, defense and rebounding, with 1-on-1 and 3-on-3 play. It costs $20; sign up by Nov. 1.$about$ where id = '5d02c8b8-34aa-47ff-aafa-11f818824011';  -- Youth basketball, grades 3-5
update public.club_events set description = $about$Fare for All sells packages of fresh produce and frozen meat once a month at Resurrection Lutheran Church, under the water tower. Packages run $10 to $30, below retail, and anyone can buy: there are no income rules and no forms. Cash, credit, debit and EBT cards are accepted.$about$ where id = 'f0432947-8a81-4884-ad4d-b47c3e5735bc';  -- Fare for All
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph's Planning Commission reviews planning and zoning matters and makes recommendations to the City Council, guided by the city's Comprehensive Plan. Its seven members, chaired by Jon Hazen, meet the second Monday of each month in the Council Chambers at the Government Center. Meetings are open to the public; the agenda is posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '8523477b-60f0-445e-b6db-11fc1da3aa78';  -- Planning Commission
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Joint Planning Board oversees development in the areas covered by the 1998 orderly annexation agreement between the City of St. Joseph and St. Joseph Township. Four members come from the city and four from the township, and the city processes land use applications for the board to review. It meets at the Government Center on the second Tuesday of the month when there is business.$about$ where id = '1e0d4348-10a1-4d64-aed8-726e292ceee8';  -- Joint Planning Board
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph Parks and Rec runs Thursday night youth volleyball at 6 and dodgeball at 7 in the Kennedy Community School gym, through Dec. 10. Both are for ages 6 to 14 and cost $20 each.$about$ where id = 'ae509bcf-50ac-4062-afd0-11390e7e2561';  -- Youth volleyball and dodgeball
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council, Mayor Adam Scepaniak and four councilmembers, meets the first and third Monday of each month at the Government Center to pass ordinances, set city policy and manage the budget. Meetings are open to the public and air live on the local cable channel. Agendas and minutes are in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '08a7966b-4ba5-42b3-8018-42b5d831eb68';  -- City Council Meeting
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council, Mayor Adam Scepaniak and four councilmembers, meets in a work session the hour before its regular meeting. The council's meetings are open to the public. Agendas and minutes are in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = 'a39a117a-3d79-4f1d-a3ec-deffd0983ae0';  -- City Council Work Session
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph's Economic Development Authority works on business recruitment, retention and expansion, infrastructure readiness, workforce development and promoting the city. Its five members are appointed by the mayor and council and meet at noon on the third Tuesday of the month at the Government Center. Past agendas note the meeting is also offered on Zoom.$about$ where id = '48fadb69-7771-411d-ad53-3ea387a8d5c9';  -- Economic Development Authority
update public.club_events set description = $about$Teams of up to four race to finish a 500-piece jigsaw puzzle, hands only, no tools. Entry is $50 per team, and each team gets a $15 Sal's gift card. Arrive early to order food before the clock starts.$about$ where id = 'b8588e8f-16a1-40b0-b540-aa4be36e550f';  -- Fall Adult Puzzle Competition
update public.club_events set description = $about$Teams of up to four race to finish a 500-piece jigsaw puzzle, hands only, no tools. Entry is $50 per team, and each team gets a $15 Sal's gift card. Arrive early to order food before the clock starts.$about$ where id = '4b4bf03e-e17f-44da-92c3-73e68f9d2a22';  -- Fall Puzzle Competition
