update public.club_events set description = $about$The Joint Planning Board oversees development in the areas covered by the 1998 orderly annexation agreement between the City of St. Joseph and St. Joseph Township. Four members come from the city and four from the township, and the city processes land use applications for the board to review. It meets at the Government Center on the second Tuesday of the month when there is business.$about$ where id = '7baa013c-5efb-4c96-b034-73b6cccccdaf';  -- Joint Planning Board
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph's Planning Commission reviews planning and zoning matters and makes recommendations to the City Council, guided by the city's Comprehensive Plan. Its seven members, chaired by Jon Hazen, meet the second Monday of each month in the Council Chambers at the Government Center. Meetings are open to the public; the agenda is posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = 'ebb7df91-6650-4df6-98a2-20b37e27389e';  -- Planning Commission
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph's Economic Development Authority is a five-member board appointed by the mayor and City Council. It works to help commercial and industrial development in town, covering business, workforce and market development along with infrastructure. Recent agendas have also offered the meeting on Zoom, and agendas and minutes are posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = 'c16ca798-7a25-4907-8fb7-567ea5088673';  -- Economic Development Authority
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council holds a work session an hour before its regular meeting. Topics are listed on the agenda the city posts ahead of time in its Agenda Center.$about$ where id = 'd462684f-f982-4129-a6d2-b8e66a892856';  -- City Council Work Session
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council holds its regular meeting, where members act on city business such as the consent agenda, bills, hires and department reports. During public comments, up to three people may speak for up to three minutes each on items not on the agenda. Recent meetings have also been offered on Zoom, with the link on the agenda posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '092a7945-504f-42f7-856b-e249ed02330a';  -- City Council Meeting
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council holds its regular meeting, where members act on city business such as the consent agenda, bills, hires and department reports. During public comments, up to three people may speak for up to three minutes each on items not on the agenda. Recent meetings have also been offered on Zoom, with the link on the agenda posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '7ed168da-473b-47aa-8e2d-df6e5fe2cecb';  -- City Council Meeting
update public.club_events set description = $about$St. Joseph's Planning Commission makes recommendations to the City Council on planning and zoning, and helps guide the city's long-term growth under its Comprehensive Plan. The seven members are appointed by the mayor and approved by the council, with Jon Hazen as chair. Agendas and meeting materials are posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = '826cc12a-9253-4fbb-8031-c8b55937ce90';  -- Planning Commission
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Joint Planning Board oversees development in the areas covered by the orderly annexation agreement between the City of St. Joseph and St. Joseph Township, first signed in 1998 and amended in 2019. Its eight members, four from the city and four from the township, review land use applications with the goal of growing the city inward and keeping farmland in farming. It meets only as needed.$about$ where id = 'bd80180a-ad69-4e93-b4b5-129b26cc2b9d';  -- Joint Planning Board
update public.club_events set description = $about$The St. Joseph City Council holds its regular meeting, where members act on city business such as the consent agenda, bills, hires and department reports. During public comments, up to three people may speak for up to three minutes each on items not on the agenda. Recent meetings have also been offered on Zoom, with the link on the agenda posted in the city's Agenda Center.$about$ where id = 'c7a2c2f5-31de-4c8a-b6d7-c27ef21a5b89';  -- City Council Meeting
