update public.club_events set description = $about$ROCORI hosts a first-round MSHSL Section 2-4A football playoff game at Blattner Stadium. The fourth-seeded Spartans face fifth-seeded St. Peter (5-3), and the winner travels to top-seeded Willmar (8-0) on Halloween.$about$ where id = '85ab2b7c-fa95-4ef7-b3ad-6edec5b53d73';  -- ROCORI Football vs St. Peter
update public.club_events set description = $about$Royalton hosts Osakis in a first-round match of the MSHSL Section 6-2A volleyball playoffs.$about$ where id = 'fc3f6775-1369-4368-821f-1ce2fdad9a50';  -- Royalton Volleyball vs Osakis
update public.club_events set description = $about$Royalton opens the MSHSL Section 6-2A football playoffs at home. The third-seeded Royals (4-4) host No. 6 seed Pillager (3-5) in the first round.$about$ where id = 'fbad563b-d0ae-48f3-8a80-49eb51944115';  -- Royalton Football vs Pillager
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's University's varsity rugby side, SJU Red, hosts North Dakota State at the Radio Towers field in Collegeville. The Johnnies are 5-0, ranked No. 11 in the National College Rugby Coaches' Poll and lead the Division III Northern Lights standings. The Northern Lights Conference finals follow on Oct. 31.$about$ where id = '67adfcba-3d43-4449-8a1a-5ee8ac462835';  -- SJU Rugby vs North Dakota State: SJU Red
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's swimming and diving hosts Macalester in an NCAA Division III MIAC dual meet at the Warner Palaestra Pool. The Johnnies come off a ninth-place finish at the MIAC vs. WIAC Invitational in Rochester, where Macalester placed sixth. The Scots edged SJU 155-143 when the teams met last year in St. Paul.$about$ where id = '96e53540-a4aa-4935-8d36-28952c589be9';  -- SJU Swimming and Diving vs Macalester
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's basketball opens its season with an exhibition against Division II St. Cloud State in Sexton Arena. It is the first meeting between the two programs since 2017, when the Johnnies won 73-67 at Halenbeck Hall. The Huskies went 26-7 last season and led the NSIC at 20-2, while SJU returns nearly all of its scoring from a team that finished second in the MIAC.$about$ where id = 'd1976cc3-a3f8-4566-a642-20592a84cbfd';  -- SJU Basketball vs St. Cloud State
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's football hosts Gustavus Adolphus in an NCAA Division III MIAC game at Clemens Stadium. The Johnnies are ranked No. 3 in the AFCA poll and unbeaten in conference play, while the Gusties have won three straight in October. Tickets are sold online by card only, and a clear bag policy is in effect: no backpacks, large purses or coolers.$about$ where id = '48dfc8c0-cb9c-4747-a0fe-6b9b802961a4';  -- SJU Football vs Gustavus Adolphus
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's cross country hosts its annual Fall Finale on its Collegeville campus, a home race for both men and women in the week before the NCAA North Regional. Last year SJU won the three-team meet over Gustavus Adolphus and Concordia-Moorhead while resting its top eight runners for regionals.$about$ where id = '517b5083-a84d-4a4d-b6d6-a61114d69058';  -- SJU Cross Country: Fall Finale
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's wrestling opens its home season in Sexton Arena with a dual against MSU Moorhead, the second match of a doubleheader that starts with Saskatchewan at 5 p.m. One ticket covers both duals.$about$ where id = 'a755f411-582d-4fad-8ace-169bbd94a762';  -- SJU Wrestling vs MSU-Moorhead
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's wrestling opens its 2026-27 season in Sexton Arena against Saskatchewan, a Canadian university team, at 5 p.m. The Johnnies then wrestle MSU Moorhead at 6 p.m., and one ticket covers both duals.$about$ where id = 'ad80a614-8ae1-4f2f-b215-5618adda099e';  -- SJU Wrestling vs Saskatchewan
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's basketball hosts Hamline in an NCAA Division III MIAC game at Sexton Arena, the first of a three-game December homestand. The Johnnies finished second in the MIAC last season and reached their sixth conference title game in seven years, and they return nearly all of their scoring.$about$ where id = '3121137f-85f0-4c78-9da5-f87c1445c0d2';  -- SJU Basketball vs Hamline
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's basketball hosts St. Olaf in an NCAA Division III MIAC Saturday afternoon game at Sexton Arena, the middle game of a three-game December homestand. SJU returns nearly all of its scoring from a team that went 11-5 in the MIAC and finished second last season.$about$ where id = 'f1effa0d-b179-4dc9-bfba-0048b1c0e9f0';  -- SJU Basketball vs St. Olaf
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's basketball hosts Buena Vista of Iowa in its only non-conference home game of the season, the last of a three-game December homestand in Sexton Arena. The Johnnies play eight of their nine non-conference games on the road, so this is a rare chance to see them against an out-of-state NCAA Division III opponent at home.$about$ where id = '10f22618-e6a9-4cd8-b868-9317dc6bf3f1';  -- SJU Basketball vs Buena Vista
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's wrestling hosts UW-Oshkosh of the WIAC in an NCAA Division III dual at Sexton Arena.$about$ where id = 'bb6c6f8c-8329-440c-9510-37920ab3cfc4';  -- SJU Wrestling vs UW-Oshkosh
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's basketball hosts Carleton in an NCAA Division III MIAC game at Sexton Arena, its first home game of 2027. The Johnnies won 70-51 at Carleton last January and finished second in the MIAC last season.$about$ where id = 'a6550daf-5f8c-4ae0-b5f0-e0458dfd71e5';  -- SJU Basketball vs Carleton
update public.club_events set description = $about$Saint John's basketball hosts Bethel in an NCAA Division III MIAC Saturday afternoon game at Sexton Arena. The Johnnies and Royals meet twice in conference play, with the rematch at Bethel closing the regular season in February.$about$ where id = '4b94f578-1f53-48b4-923d-7eea5b24339a';  -- SJU Basketball vs Bethel
update public.club_events set description = $about$An online information session from Saint John's School of Theology and Seminary about Conversatio, a tuition-free Master of Divinity program for people discerning parish ministry or diocesan leadership. Students study theology, serve weekly in a rural parish in youth ministry, liturgy or faith formation, and grow in intercultural skills rooted in the Benedictine practice of Conversatio Morum. Staff cover the application, costs and curriculum; registration is required.$about$ where id = '06e7a680-9647-41c1-be80-311c66cd7fd4';  -- Conversatio Webinar
update public.club_events set description = $about$An online information session from Saint John's School of Theology and Seminary about the Virgil Michel Scholars program, which lets full-time residential students earn a Master of Theological Studies with a full-tuition scholarship and on-campus housing support. Named for Dom Virgil Michel, a Saint John's Abbey monk, the program suits students aiming for doctoral study. Staff cover the application, costs and curriculum; registration is required.$about$ where id = '41a18ac2-2d01-476b-8b47-8fa0b38f05ba';  -- Virgil Michel Scholars Webinar
update public.club_events set description = $about$An online information session from Saint John's School of Theology and Seminary about its Certificate in Benedictine Spirituality, a 15-credit program on the Rule of Saint Benedict and the history of Benedictine life, offered online, in person or hybrid. It is aimed at Benedictine oblates, vowed monastics and people in Benedictine mission work, and oblates and monastics get a discounted rate. Staff cover the application, costs and curriculum; registration is required.$about$ where id = '74a60b5d-857b-4ba8-a5f8-f34550a2805f';  -- Benedictine Spirituality Certificate
update public.club_events set description = $about$Sal's Bar and Grill hosts bingo every Tuesday evening. A $15 packet covers 11 games, and games 1 and 6 each pay a guaranteed $500. Proceeds support Waite Park Babe Ruth Baseball and Softball.$about$ where id = '58dd5bb5-94a6-42d7-9240-c2492b62201a';  -- Bingo Night
update public.club_events set description = $about$Friday evenings at Sal's bring Keys for Cash, which patrons sign up for at the bar, along with a meat raffle. Each round's winner gets a $30 St. Joe Meat Market gift card, and this week's raffle proceeds go to Resurrection Lutheran Church.$about$ where id = '9d6d3d58-c1fc-4b9c-8136-aa6c9c2deee4';  -- Keys for Cash & Meat Raffle
update public.club_events set description = $about$Divers from across the Central Lakes Conference compete in the diving portion of the girls swimming and diving conference championship, hosted by Sartell. The swimming events follow on Saturday. Host Sartell comes in as the newly crowned Class A True Team state champion, the program's first.$about$ where id = '5335e128-5d43-4d3d-a68f-86f9bf308af9';  -- Central Lakes Conference Diving Meet
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Central Lakes Conference girls swimming championship, hosted by Sartell, brings the conference's teams together for the swimming events after diving on Thursday. Host Sartell comes in fresh off its first Class A True Team state championship on Oct. 17, when it edged Visitation by 20 points.$about$ where id = '688507e4-cebc-421f-b443-22a157b83fab';  -- Central Lakes Conference Swim Meet
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Sartell-Sauk Rapids Storm'n Sabres, a girls hockey co-op of the two schools, open their season at home against Fergus Falls. Dan Marod, promoted from assistant in September, coaches his first game as head coach. The team is young this year, with only five upperclassmen and a large sophomore class after nine players graduated.$about$ where id = '5c875e25-4de8-4c7f-94cd-fa8126cc69fa';  -- Sartell-Sauk Rapids Girls Hockey vs Fergus Falls
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Sartell-Sauk Rapids Storm'n Sabres, the two schools' girls hockey co-op, host Thief River Falls. It is an early-season game for a young team under first-year head coach Dan Marod, with only five upperclassmen on the roster.$about$ where id = 'b3430a13-a37e-441f-abd7-427b95fa61d4';  -- Sartell-Sauk Rapids Girls Hockey vs Thief River Falls
update public.club_events set description = $about$Sauk Rapids-Rice, the No. 4 seed, hosts No. 5 Bemidji in the first round of the MSHSL Section 8-5A football playoffs. The Storm (2-6) beat the Lumberjacks 48-35 in Bemidji on Sept. 25, and Bemidji is still winless. The winner plays at top seed Brainerd on Oct. 31.$about$ where id = 'e570c6e2-a751-496a-9bcf-48b0a9d1bcc4';  -- Sauk Rapids-Rice Football vs Bemidji
update public.club_events set description = $about$The Sisters of Saint Benedict's Monastery mark the anniversary of the dedication of Sacred Heart Chapel, completed in 1914 and consecrated in 1943 once the mortgage was paid. The public is welcome to Morning Prayer at 8:15 a.m., Eucharist at 11 a.m. and Evening Prayer at 5 p.m. The celebration begins Friday at 7 p.m. with Evening Prayer, a procession, candle lighting and incense.$about$ where id = 'aa551cce-eed1-490d-9770-fa3087454662';  -- Sacred Heart Chapel Anniversary
update public.club_events set description = $about$Cathedral Middle and High School's annual winter fundraiser gala, held at the Park Event Center. The evening features entertainment from Deuces Wild Dueling Pianos, including Cathedral alum Ted Manderfeld, and tickets, tables and sponsorships are sold online.$about$ where id = '7d9bac5b-154a-4ec3-9848-3308031840b3';  -- Cathedral Winter Gala
update public.club_events set description = $about$Catholic Community Schools opens its doors for a week of open houses at its elementary schools and Cathedral Middle and High School, a chance for families considering Catholic school to tour and meet staff. Open houses run during the school day all week.$about$ where id = 'c9289d73-ae0e-4ebf-a352-3eb1805a1ab2';  -- Open House Week
update public.club_events set description = $about$Sunny Mary Meadow, the flower farm Liz Fiedler Mergen runs on her family's farm outside St. Joseph, holds an indoor farmers market in its Bloom Room event space on Tuesday afternoons through Dec. 22. Local vendors set up inside, and the farm store is open too.$about$ where id = '96558630-4f44-4937-bb3a-9d5f2eb8935f';  -- Indoor Farmers Market
update public.club_events set description = $about$The MSHSL Section 6A girls swimming and diving meet runs three days at St. Cloud Tech, with the top finishers moving on to the Class A state meet. The section includes Albany, Holdingford, Little Falls, Melrose, Rocori, Sartell-St. Stephen, Sauk Centre, Sauk Rapids-Rice, St. Cloud Apollo and St. Cloud Tech. Sartell won last year's title by five points over Melrose, and the 2026 race is expected to be close. Day one of three.$about$ where id = 'f423bac4-f10c-49e0-95f1-35dc3c2d0a00';  -- Section 6A Girls Swim Meet
update public.club_events set description = $about$The MSHSL Section 6A girls swimming and diving meet runs three days at St. Cloud Tech, with the top finishers moving on to the Class A state meet. The section includes Albany, Holdingford, Little Falls, Melrose, Rocori, Sartell-St. Stephen, Sauk Centre, Sauk Rapids-Rice, St. Cloud Apollo and St. Cloud Tech. Sartell won last year's title by five points over Melrose, and the 2026 race is expected to be close. Day two of three.$about$ where id = '416fd637-0c49-4245-a101-fc6f8a1dad7a';  -- Section 6A Girls Swim Meet
update public.club_events set description = $about$The MSHSL Section 6A girls swimming and diving meet runs three days at St. Cloud Tech, with the top finishers moving on to the Class A state meet. The section includes Albany, Holdingford, Little Falls, Melrose, Rocori, Sartell-St. Stephen, Sauk Centre, Sauk Rapids-Rice, St. Cloud Apollo and St. Cloud Tech. Sartell won last year's title by five points over Melrose, and the 2026 race is expected to be close. Final day.$about$ where id = 'a9ebc765-a0f7-4417-b28a-98aaba61ca39';  -- Section 6A Girls Swim Meet
update public.club_events set description = $about$An after-hours shopping night at White Peony Boutique, the size-inclusive women's clothing shop in downtown St. Joseph, with treats, permanent jewelry and a costume contest with prizes. It is part of the shop's Bootique Week, a week of Halloween fun, treats and surprises in store and online.$about$ where id = '0d6377b7-01dd-401d-a8ea-e1ba1098e155';  -- Boo-tique Bash
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique, WR Home Company and Obbink Distilling host Twinkle & Toast, a private, ticketed holiday evening at both downtown St. Joseph shops. Tickets are $35 and include a holiday gift to take home, a festive drink from Obbink Distilling, treats and private holiday shopping among twinkle lights and Christmas scents. Tickets are limited.$about$ where id = 'a85c84a6-11a7-4135-a7b3-81dffa985c9c';  -- Twinkle & Toast
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique, Lindsay Salzbrun's size-inclusive women's clothing shop in downtown St. Joseph, kicks off the holidays with a two-day launch of brand-new holiday arrivals and festive favorites. The shop is open 9 a.m. to 4 p.m. Saturday and 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. Sunday for the launch.$about$ where id = 'ca01d3cd-b5ac-40fe-902d-2bfa19d3bb71';  -- White Peony Holiday Launch
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique, Lindsay Salzbrun's size-inclusive women's clothing shop in downtown St. Joseph, kicks off the holidays with a two-day launch of brand-new holiday arrivals and festive favorites. The shop is open 9 a.m. to 4 p.m. Saturday and 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. Sunday for the launch.$about$ where id = '908046be-d9bf-419a-b3ec-eca6e34b202b';  -- Style Hunt Holiday Launch
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique runs 12 Days of Giving online from Nov. 9 to 20, with a new deal each day plus new arrivals, giveaways and surprises along the way.$about$ where id = 'b4805523-46a2-4a6e-92b6-c658263d03f6';  -- 12 Days of Giving
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique opens early for Pink Friday, a growing national movement that encourages shopping at local small businesses a week before Black Friday. The shop invites neighbors to shop small first and start the holiday season by supporting businesses in their own community.$about$ where id = '734cbc1c-c667-4d43-8dd8-014c890859d2';  -- Pink Friday
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique opens early for Pink Friday, a growing national movement that encourages shopping at local small businesses a week before Black Friday. The shop invites neighbors to shop small first and start the holiday season by supporting businesses in their own community.$about$ where id = 'c3049c42-2317-4ce3-8b64-373c542700b8';  -- Pink Friday
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique, the size-inclusive women's clothing shop in downtown St. Joseph, opens early on Black Friday with deals, specials and surprises throughout the day.$about$ where id = 'c3320e6c-06a9-436d-b8d5-f0f09dad1e95';  -- Black Friday
update public.club_events set description = $about$White Peony Boutique marks Shop Small Saturday by inviting shoppers to spend the day in St. Joe, stopping by the boutique and visiting the other small businesses downtown to shop, eat and support local.$about$ where id = '70e28058-abc1-406d-841f-fa3b6f463073';  -- Shop Small Saturday
update public.club_events set description = $about$WR Home & Clothing Co., the home decor and women's clothing boutique co-owned by Shantel Waytashek and Kendra Harlander in St. Joseph's old fire and police building, kicks off the holidays with an open house. Doors open early for a day of holiday decor, cozy textures, thoughtful gifts and new seasonal collections.$about$ where id = '42fb50e5-820b-44de-a6b6-bcec2337e55d';  -- Holiday Open House
update public.club_events set description = $about$WR Home & Clothing Co., the home decor and women's clothing boutique co-owned by Shantel Waytashek and Kendra Harlander in St. Joseph's old fire and police building, kicks off the holidays with an open house. Doors open early for a day of holiday decor, cozy textures, thoughtful gifts and new seasonal collections.$about$ where id = '25cddc6b-7649-42b2-a85f-50c04ed3272a';  -- Holiday Open House
update public.clubs set description = $about$St. Joseph's American Legion, the John Kuebelbeck Post, was chartered in 1919 and is named for a sergeant of the 362nd Infantry in World War I. Veterans of every branch, and current service members, are welcome at the monthly membership meeting. The Post also hosts bingo and 500 cards, and its Auxiliary and Sons of the American Legion meet there too, gathering things like Christmas gift bags for the VA.$about$ where id = 'b0e9ce81-18ae-42ce-9e75-bf503ad2da45';  -- American Legion Post 328
update public.clubs set description = $about$Twice a month, volunteers at the St. Joseph Laundromat hand out quarters, detergent and dryer sheets so neighbors can wash and dry for free. The Central Minnesota Catholic Worker started it here in 2022 with the laundromat's owner, and parishioners of the Benedictine Catholic Communities staff the nights. There are no eligibility rules and little paperwork. In the year to August 2026 they covered 910 loads.$about$ where id = '53885668-4f6e-46ac-a660-e40ca58d01fc';  -- Laundry Love
update public.clubs set description = $about$Knitters, crocheters and quilters gather Wednesday mornings in Resurrection Lutheran's Fellowship Hall until noon. They make prayer shawls for people needing extra prayer, a baby blanket for every baby baptized at the church, afghans, mittens, scarves, wee hats and bandages for the military. Finished pieces go to Lutheran World Relief, the People's Church and the Linus Project, and gifts of cotton fabric and yarn are welcome.$about$ where id = '4682c5d0-a1e0-41ab-bafb-41c4c10cfc30';  -- The Yarnovers
update public.clubs set description = $about$Recognized by the state since 1954, the St. Joe Rod and Gun Club keeps up lake access at Kraemer, Watab and Rassier Lakes and has taught firearms safety since 1972. Dues are $30 a year, April to March, and bring use of the club's private launch ramps and a vote on club business, with the money going to lake care and youth outdoor education. Monthly meetings end with door prize drawings, and family events include the Birdhouse Build and a February ice fishing contest.$about$ where id = '2e8db1f0-2090-407d-885f-b9fb7e8e01b4';  -- St. Joe Rod and Gun Club
update public.places set about = $about$Daisy A Day Floral & Gift is a flower and gift shop on College Avenue, owned by Tracy Omann-Smith. She opened it in 1996, inspired by her mother, Renee Omann, who started the first Daisy A Day in Sartell in 1992; the two shops shared a name but were separate businesses. The shop makes arrangements for everyday occasions, holidays, weddings and funerals, and delivers around the area.$about$ where id = '23dd1b61-a5ae-4fb3-bb1e-af98c921ae55';  -- Daisy A Day Floral & Gift
update public.places set about = $about$Magnifi Financial is a member owned, not-for-profit financial cooperative in Minnesota that provides low cost loans, checking, savings, online services and more.$about$ where id = '805fce4e-79c4-428b-bbb2-ec2799fcaf82';  -- Magnifi Financial
update public.places set about = $about$Flour & Flower is a from-scratch bakery and flower shop downtown, founded by chef Erin Lucas, who runs it with her partner Mateo Mackbee. It opened in May 2020 and bakes sweet and savory pastries daily, using local ingredients when it can. Pies are the specialty, a nod to Erin's grandmother, alongside turnovers, croissants and artisan breads. It also sells fair-trade coffee and bouquets grown in Central Minnesota.$about$ where id = 'fed769b6-ec34-4cc6-bb05-8e7016e79aec';  -- Flour & Flower
update public.places set about = $about$Groundsman is a St. Joseph outdoor services company started in 2020 by owner Tanner Kier. It handles landscaping, lawn care and seasonal cleanups for homes, and in winter plows driveways and clears snow in St. Joseph, Sartell, St. Cloud and Cold Spring.$about$ where id = '13db727c-f385-43ab-a67d-8cb534833563';  -- Groundsman LLC
update public.places set about = $about$Coborn's in St. Joseph is a full grocery store on Elm Street with produce, meat, deli, bakery and floral departments, plus a pharmacy, Caribou Coffee, a liquor store and dry cleaning drop-off under one roof. Coborn's started in Sauk Rapids in 1921 and is employee-owned, still led by the Coborn family. Shoppers can buy in store or order online for pickup or delivery.$about$ where id = 'cbd3dec1-e1ed-4aa7-b32d-a02f7ae4ff8d';  -- Coborn's Grocery Store
update public.places set about = $about$St. Joseph Veterinary Clinic is a multi-doctor practice on East Minnesota Street that cares for dogs and cats as well as exotics, birds, reptiles and pocket pets. It is part of the Cold Spring, St. Joseph and Paynesville clinics, which have served Central Minnesota since 1951. The clinic has surgery rooms, radiology, a lab, a pharmacy and kennels for dogs and cats.$about$ where id = 'c9038816-1498-4bf2-8724-d726040b608c';  -- St. Joseph Veterinary Clinic
update public.places set about = $about$John Kuebelbeck American Legion Post 328 is St. Joseph's veterans post, chartered in 1919 and named for Sgt. John Kuebelbeck of the 362nd Infantry, the first St. Joseph soldier killed in World War I. Veterans from every branch and current service members can join; members meet monthly. The post's bar is open to the public daily, and it hosts bingo, card games, its Auxiliary and Sons of the Legion, and rents its hall for events.$about$ where id = 'b8088f9f-a0b8-44ee-a63c-6242e10fe4d8';  -- John Kuebelbeck American Legion Post 328
update public.places set about = $about$Omann Insurance Agency is a family-run independent agency that has served the St. Cloud area since 1948, with offices in St. Joseph, Sartell and Waite Park. It writes auto, home, farm, commercial and umbrella coverage. The St. Joseph office on Cedar Street is led by agent Peter Omann.$about$ where id = 'a6e854dd-632e-4e84-a6e5-2ce40c753af5';  -- Omann Insurance Agency, LLC
update public.places set about = $about$Home Town Title is a locally owned title company that has helped Minnesota homeowners close on homes since 1998. It handles closings, title insurance and escrow for buyers, sellers and refinances, with offices in St. Joseph, Sauk Centre and Alexandria. The St. Joseph office is in the St. Joseph Business Center on County Road 75, and the team offers after-hours and short-notice closings.$about$ where id = '71571e13-d608-48c8-8755-f3e78bb391a8';  -- Home Town Title
update public.places set about = $about$Family-owned tire shop & auto repair in St. Joseph, MN, proudly serving Saint Cloud & Central Minnesota since 1980.$about$ where id = '10d6b505-b952-4b17-a1ba-64b7affe7338';  -- TireMaxx Service Centers
update public.places set about = $about$St. Joseph's post office on West Ash Street handles mailing, shipping, stamps and P.O. boxes for town. In 2024 the Postal Service honored retail associate Jill Soltis for more than 30 years at the counter here.$about$ where id = '43d7228e-1fe5-487a-a30a-f53065818e22';  -- United States Postal Service
update public.places set about = $about$Kensington Bank is a privately owned Minnesota bank. Its St. Joseph office on First Avenue NW opened in 2023 in a sleek renovated building after the bank left downtown St. Cloud. It is a loan and deposit office rather than a teller branch: staff open accounts and make loans, and an ATM on site handles deposits and withdrawals.$about$ where id = 'b21d44d8-e28f-4b4e-8a7d-65eed035eb31';  -- Kensington Bank
update public.places set about = $about$AMS Tax & Accounting Solutions is a local CPA firm on Cedar Street, founded in 2023 by owner Aaron Smith, a CPA since 2009 who has worked in Central Minnesota his whole career. The firm does tax preparation and planning, bookkeeping, payroll, business consulting and retirement and business transition planning. It works with farms, restaurants and bars, builders, retailers and real estate and transportation businesses.$about$ where id = '5be29c95-5f5d-45aa-83b0-0f591916b4ee';  -- AMS Tax & Accounting Solutions, PA
update public.places set about = $about$Joetown Burgers serves smashed burgers, fries and old-school milkshakes inside The House Food and Tap, the food hall on Second Avenue NW. It is run by chefs Erin Lucas and Mateo Mackbee, the pair behind Flour & Flower, and opened in 2025.$about$ where id = 'd2737fe2-749c-4473-8346-35b2c5c774b0';  -- Joetown Burgers
update public.places set about = $about$Granite City Gymnastics teaches recreational and competitive gymnastics for kids, from preschool classes to Xcel and developmental teams. Owners Tommy and Amy Rodine opened it in Waite Park about 2007 with 44 students and grew to some 450 before moving into a new 12,000-square-foot gym in St. Joseph's industrial park in 2023. It also runs open gyms, private lessons and birthday parties.$about$ where id = '432e41ab-313d-4d88-b891-08e42ab95b69';  -- Granite City Gymnastics
update public.places set about = $about$Thomsens Garden Center is a large greenhouse and garden center in rural St. Joseph, started in the late 1970s by Bob and Bonnie Thomsen. Ryan and Steph Roder, St. Ben's and St. John's alumni, bought it in 2022. Thomsens grows much of what it sells: annuals, perennials, vegetables, herbs, shrubs and trees, plus soil, mulch and pots. It also offers container and landscape design, delivery, and classes like its spring hanging-basket party.$about$ where id = 'f97e06d6-8cf9-4a75-9acd-b891ba516509';  -- Thomsen's Garden Center
update public.places set about = $about$Unwind is a holistic healing center founded in 2013 by Brittney, a craniosacral therapist, lactation consultant and doula. It offers craniosacral therapy and myofascial release for infants through adults, breastfeeding support, full-spectrum doula care and wellness coaching. Unwind also holds free infant clinics and teaches bodywork classes, with locations in St. Joseph, Alexandria and Fargo.$about$ where id = 'e945c8d1-4575-4151-a415-db3403b0c54b';  -- Unwind: Collaborative Healing Center
update public.places set about = $about$Amy Hedtke runs the State Farm agency on 8th Avenue NE, which she opened in 2021. She and her team help people with auto, home, renters, condo and life insurance and recreational coverage, and a Spanish-speaking account manager serves Spanish-speaking neighbors. Amy came to the area for the College of Saint Benedict, where she earned her degree in 2005 and captained the women's hockey team.$about$ where id = 'cf3c7388-f4ab-4522-ae1d-3d2a018c69a5';  -- Amy Hedtke - State Farm
update public.places set about = $about$Hansen & Company Woodworks builds custom cabinets, architectural millwork and stone surfaces for commercial construction, mostly apartment and multi-family projects. Adam Hansen founded it in 2004, and everything is engineered and made in St. Joseph. In 2026 it opened a 92,000-square-foot plant with what it calls North America's first fully automated frameless batch-one cabinet line. Visits are by appointment.$about$ where id = '5acceae4-ff09-40c7-9c46-e05d2857f018';  -- Hansen & Company Woodworks
update public.places set about = $about$Lee's Ace Hardware is the hardware store on Cedar Street, part of the Ace Hardware network. Directory listings name Lee Wolf as owner and date the store to 1982.$about$ where id = 'a5cd14e5-24b9-4d32-b57f-accb06cfdf1c';  -- Lee's Ace Hardware
update public.places set about = $about$RJ's Auto Repair is a small, long-running car repair shop on 115th Avenue in rural St. Joseph. Business listings date it to 1986.$about$ where id = 'b370e75b-0fcc-41be-91df-0b26b41e76a2';  -- RJ's Auto Repair
update public.places set about = $about$All Occasion Floral & Gifts is a family-owned flower shop on Birch Street, with the entrance in back, run for more than 22 years. It designs sympathy and funeral pieces, wedding and event flowers, and everyday bouquets, and makes daily deliveries to local funeral homes and hospitals. The shop also carries green and blooming plants, gift baskets, chocolates, candles and balloons.$about$ where id = 'ab44fdd8-302b-4523-abca-d087d89874f1';  -- All Occasion Floral & Gifts
update public.places set about = $about$White Peony Boutique is a women's clothing shop with size-inclusive styles from XS to 3X, owned by Lindsay Salzbrun. She started it in her basement in 2018 and opened the St. Joseph store in 2022 in the former police station on 1st Avenue NW. The boutique gets new arrivals each week, holds live online sales, and hosts the Peony Market with local vendors.$about$ where id = '606a751d-98e2-4f3a-8926-a1d3966592e0';  -- White Peony Boutique
update public.places set about = $about$Hair by Hanna is a hair salon on West Minnesota Street run by stylist Hanna, offering cuts, color, styling and extensions. Appointments are booked through Vagaro.$about$ where id = '8e61e7d8-f5aa-426e-9325-bebb2875cae9';  -- Hair By Hanna
update public.places set about = $about$Floral Arts is a family-owned florist on 1st Avenue NE that has served St. Joseph and St. Cloud since 1968. It is known for sympathy designs and also does weddings, events and arrangements for every occasion, with same-day delivery in St. Joseph.$about$ where id = 'c10adb95-4e83-4b9a-95c5-f96178dad197';  -- Floral Arts Inc.
update public.places set about = $about$Bo Diddley's Deli opened on College Avenue in 1981 and is known for big sub sandwiches on bread baked fresh daily, meat sliced in house and homemade soup. Lee Weisbrich, a longtime customer, bought it from founder John Forsythe in 2018 and kept the menu. A 2022 remodel added an outdoor patio. There are also shops in St. Cloud and Eden Prairie.$about$ where id = 'dcc05e93-f05b-4143-b05c-d2a665bf72f2';  -- Bo Diddley's Deli
update public.places set about = $about$China One is a Chinese restaurant in the shopping strip on County Road 75, serving dine-in and takeout.$about$ where id = 'fa4b334d-2a48-4f99-94eb-1ac8ea764367';  -- China One
update public.places set about = $about$Gary's Pizza has made pizza in downtown St. Joseph since Gary Schyma opened it in 1982 at Minnesota Street and College Avenue. Roger Steichen, who worked there in high school, bought it in 1988 at age 19 and grew it to four locations. Dough is made fresh daily and the sauce is the shop's own recipe. The menu also has wings, pasta, flatbreads and salads, with dine-in, pickup and delivery.$about$ where id = '971d058c-e779-44e5-a133-bd4fc2d08b8b';  -- Gary's Pizza
update public.places set about = $about$Coborn's Pharmacy fills prescriptions inside the Coborn's grocery store on Elm Street, so neighbors can pick up medicine and groceries in one stop. Coborn's is an employee-owned Central Minnesota grocer that started in Sauk Rapids in 1921.$about$ where id = '0ad2d330-9895-4735-9ff1-44c8b1d43b31';  -- Coborn's Pharmacy
update public.places set about = $about$Insurance Advisors is an insurance agency on Birch Street offering auto, home, life and health coverage. Listings date it to 1996.$about$ where id = 'eec1f213-8624-4b14-9b00-2a5285e306df';  -- Insurance Advisors
update public.places set about = $about$Kay's Kitchen is a hometown diner on College Avenue, built in 1972 by Kay and "Dirk" Dierkhising and known for its pies. It has stayed in the family: Kay's great-nephew Dan Kuebelbeck, a longtime baker there, and Ashley Blonigen took over in 2022 from Tanya Finken, who had run it since 2009.$about$ where id = 'c109060a-ab8c-4197-bfc6-0d6cda06c964';  -- Kay's Kitchen
update public.places set about = $about$Blush Salon is an upscale salon and suites run by owner Nicole Springer, who founded it in Waite Park in 2015 and moved it to St. Joseph's old Ford dealership building in 2025. Its team of independent stylists does precision cuts, color, extensions and styling, and suites in the building offer services such as massage and waxing.$about$ where id = '2b90146d-3652-4a02-b1a5-a5d132c62522';  -- Blush Salon
update public.places set about = $about$Bello Cucina is an Italian steakhouse in downtown St. Joseph, opened in 2012 by chef and owner Jason Mueller. The menu centers on steaks, chops and fish alongside traditional pastas, and it has been voted best Italian restaurant in Central Minnesota ten years running. There is an outdoor patio, and the restaurant sells imported olive oils and infused balsamic vinegars. Reservations are encouraged.$about$ where id = 'a36c5d37-f384-477b-b601-7f535b2ea7fd';  -- Bello Cucina | Italian
update public.places set about = $about$Brenny Transportation is a trucking and logistics company headquartered in St. Joseph, founded in 1996 by Joyce and Todd Brenny in a small Waite Park office with three employees. Both started their careers behind the wheel. Brenny hauls freight across the country, from long-haul to last-mile delivery, and offers warehousing for manufacturers, distributors, retailers and individuals.$about$ where id = '2e89bbb6-8728-4ae6-8b8b-53c1629ba395';  -- Brenny Transportation, Inc.
update public.places set about = $about$The Perfect Fit is Julia Krengel's practice in Muscle Activation Techniques (MAT), a hands-on method for people with muscle pain, limited mobility or chronic tension. Julia, a certified personal trainer for more than 20 years, started the business in 2015 and has practiced MAT for eight years. She works out of St. Joseph Health & Wellness on 1st Avenue NW.$about$ where id = '8cd01a3f-1441-4c1d-9aef-81419a6a75f0';  -- The Perfect Fit, LLC
update public.places set about = $about$Little Saints Academy is a locally owned child care center on 1st Avenue SE caring for infants through preschoolers, with a musical flair. It has served families since 2010, with daily routines and hands-on learning to get kids ready for kindergarten. Owner Amy Bonfig leads a staff that includes many longtime teachers.$about$ where id = 'd66e9cbf-d9d8-48e1-8fdf-412c8cf8202d';  -- Little Saints Academy
update public.places set about = $about$Founded in 2000, privately owned and based in St. Joseph, MN, Autobody 2000 has over 30 years of experience in all areas of vehicle body and glass repair.$about$ where id = '2f68442e-0399-4ac5-b60d-cc3237fa7746';  -- Autobody 2000 Inc
update public.places set about = $about$Cedar Street Salon & Spa is an Aveda salon on Cedar Street offering cuts, color and styling, along with spa services such as skin care, facials, waxing, manicures and pedicures. Its stylists help with anything from a full new look to a refresh, and chairs are available to rent.$about$ where id = 'ffc8cb61-7783-4676-9e3d-ba8bc813b718';  -- Cedar Street Salon & Spa
update public.places set about = $about$The Gorecki Gallery is in the Benedicta Arts Center at the College of Saint Benedict, the campus arts building that also houses the art, music, theater and dance departments. The center opened in 1964 and is named for Mother Benedicta Riepp, foundress of the Benedictine women in the United States. A 2006 renovation, led by a gift from Ben and Dorothy Gorecki, gave the gallery its name.$about$ where id = 'cc5cf7ef-2f3a-477f-a1e2-f26c4fd4178e';  -- CSB Benedicta Arts Center Galleries (Gorecki Gallery)
update public.places set about = $about$Bad Habit Brewing is a craft brewery and taproom on College Avenue, opened in 2015 by home brewer Aaron Rieland and four partners. In 2019 it moved into its current building with a taproom and a large outdoor patio. It pours its own beer and seltzers plus THC-infused drinks, sells to-go, and rents space for private events.$about$ where id = '3f3c5259-67f9-491e-9af5-5c4b21a80b58';  -- Bad Habit Brewing Company
update public.places set about = $about$Sal's has been a downtown St. Joseph gathering place since Marcellus "Sal" and Margaret Schneider opened Sal's Cafe in 1946 with help from their twelve children. Their son Dale and his wife Diane "Bip" Schneider took over in 1971 and renamed it Sal's Bar & Grill, and later generations of the family still run it. The kitchen makes its own buns and soups to go with classic bar food, and the crowd mixes locals, college students and alumni.$about$ where id = '6b0f79a9-fff6-4e60-af98-a6a45ce51223';  -- Sal's Bar & Grill
update public.places set about = $about$The Estates Bed & Breakfast sits on the east end of St. Joseph's downtown, close to both colleges. It has three themed suites, the Bennie, the Johnnie and the Minnesota, each with a private bath, and guests can also rent the whole house. Visiting families and returning CSB and SJU alumni are a big part of its guests.$about$ where id = 'afb922c5-2d75-4704-8179-5c6043323627';  -- The Estates Bed & Breakfast
update public.places set about = $about$Bruno Press is a women-owned letterpress print shop in St. Joseph run by printmaker Mary Bruno. Every piece is made by hand with carved linoleum blocks and hand-set wood and metal type, from funny greeting cards to posters and fine art prints. The shop also hosts print parties, workshops and kids' collaborations.$about$ where id = '443332c9-0465-49f3-9afc-f5f103eb3bad';  -- Bruno Press
update public.places set about = $about$Trobec's Bus Service has run school buses and charters in the St. Cloud area for more than 75 years. Its fleet carries students to school, on field trips and to games, and its motor coaches take groups to weddings, family reunions, corporate events and team trips across central Minnesota.$about$ where id = '75afbf0c-cb83-462b-8d38-5890d9cd0f06';  -- Trobec's Bus Service, Inc.
update public.places set about = $about$Floor to Ceiling is a flooring and design center in St. Joseph that sells and installs carpet, hardwood, laminate, vinyl and tile, along with blinds, shades, shutters and drapery. It has served central Minnesota for more than 40 years and offers in-home measuring and estimates, and it recently opened a new showroom on 21st Ave NE.$about$ where id = 'f974053c-c39a-4bb3-a6ef-bf163d232b7f';  -- Floor to Ceiling
update public.places set about = $about$Central MN Realty is a family-owned real estate company that helps people buy and sell homes across central Minnesota. It has offices in towns from St. Cloud and Alexandria to Melrose and Little Falls, and its St. Joseph office sits on College Avenue downtown.$about$ where id = '3a9a0946-ad17-4d83-9883-6f245a032569';  -- Central MN Realty
update public.places set about = $about$CMS Autobody is a body shop on Cedar Street that repairs all makes of cars and trucks. Its crew handles collision repair, paintless dent repair for hail damage, semi truck body work, and motorhome and RV repair, and it also does custom parts and paint for cars and motorcycles.$about$ where id = '20b5fabb-0c41-438d-840a-ce8da5d6d6e4';  -- CMS Autobody
update public.places set about = $about$The Wandering Cow is a family-friendly ice cream shop in downtown St. Joseph run by Daryl and Heidi Schaefer. It scoops Chocolate Shoppe ice cream and serves shaved ice and made-to-order shakes. Its ice cream trucks also cater parties, graduations, weddings and community events.$about$ where id = '01ed0060-197a-4ce3-bfb4-a15ba1777285';  -- The Wandering Cow Ice Cream
update public.places set about = $about$Obbink Distilling is a space-themed distillery and cocktail room on Date Street, opened in June 2023 by St. John's alumni. It is named for Gregg Obbink, a retired satellite engineer who worked on NASA projects and developed a method that ages whiskey in days instead of years. Along with whiskey, it makes gin and vodka and serves seasonal craft cocktails and non-alcoholic drinks, and it hosts classes and events.$about$ where id = '00041f04-ca31-4c78-83d2-0c99dc78cb8b';  -- Obbink Distilling
update public.places set about = $about$Woodcrest of Country Manor is a senior living community on the Country Manor campus, offering assisted living suites, apartments and home health care. It sits on wooded land with flower and vegetable gardens, a bird sanctuary and walking trails. Country Manor has cared for seniors in the area for more than 50 years.$about$ where id = '1b601b20-6069-41bb-81dc-07ce8f3c65e1';  -- Woodcrest of Country Manor
update public.places set about = $about$Chiropractic Connection is Dr. Keith Schleper's chiropractic clinic on County Road 75. Along with chiropractic care for patients from babies to adults, it offers massage therapy, auto accident care, shock wave therapy and wellness and weight loss programs.$about$ where id = 'c29f89a1-5caa-423a-9424-b08373328871';  -- Chiropractic Connection, PC
update public.places set about = $about$The House Food & Tap is a community food hall in downtown St. Joseph where several local kitchens share one roof, serving burgers, wraps and salads, brick-oven pizza and specialty coffee. It has a 30-tap self-pour wall, and it was shaped by hundreds of ideas from St. Joseph residents who wanted a place to gather. The hall also supports chefs who are just getting started.$about$ where id = '7a27d0a0-126d-412c-871d-20a531a8ba72';  -- The House Food and Tap
update public.places set about = $about$Golden Hour is a tanning and wellness studio on Ash Street. It offers classic tanning beds, UVB and red light hybrid beds and spray tans, plus an infrared sauna, Celluma light therapy, compression therapy, Raindrop Massage and muscle testing. A small shop sells clean beauty and wellness products.$about$ where id = '21e97746-5906-433f-8322-76fdb267b86a';  -- Golden Hour Tanning
update public.places set about = $about$Uptown Styles is a full-service hair salon on Minnesota Street downtown that works with natural, holistic and organic products. It offers cuts, color and highlights, hair treatments and facial waxing, and every visit starts with a consultation. It is the St. Joseph location of Michelle Meier's Arbor salon in Waite Park.$about$ where id = '32654a5c-2f31-460d-b750-fe559b7f3d4c';  -- Uptown Styles
update public.places set about = $about$Heim-kins Rescued Treasures is an antique and vintage shop on Cedar Street, run by co-owner Pat Kaeter since around 2010. It is filled with one-of-a-kind finds, jewelry, and home and garden decor, and much of its business comes from summer travelers.$about$ where id = '0afa5fe5-4429-482c-9a66-1babcadb17ab';  -- Heim-kins Rescued Treasures
update public.places set about = $about$Her Hair Studio is Hannah Remenar's salon in downtown St. Joseph, where she cuts and colors hair for new and returning clients. She has worked in the industry for nearly a decade, follows the latest color and cut trends, and aims to keep every visit comfortable and welcoming.$about$ where id = '4600a722-e962-4182-ad2a-035c04de3b74';  -- Her Hair Studio
update public.places set about = $about$Hudson & Company is a women's clothing and accessories boutique that opened in June 2021 in the restored corner building at College Avenue and Minnesota Street, which began in 1900 as Frank X. Timmer's Saloon and General Store. Owner Ann Hudson also runs NEAR + NORTH boutiques. The shop carries home decor and gifts, including pieces from local artists and vendors.$about$ where id = '339de4f9-8cdb-4e9c-8a4d-5a21ea96f86a';  -- Hudson & Company
update public.places set about = $about$Pierce Insurance is an independent agency that shops several carriers for home, auto, commercial, health, life and umbrella coverage. David Pierce started it in Litchfield in 1974, and since 2022 it has been owned by his grandson Tim Pierce and longtime agent Troy Atkinson. It opened its St. Joseph office downtown on 2nd Ave NW in 2025.$about$ where id = 'b4af59d7-0006-4fb7-8ff9-b79bb2e380c4';  -- Pierce Insurance Agency
update public.places set about = $about$Hollander's St. Joseph Liquor Shoppe is the off-sale liquor store on Cedar Street, selling beer, wine and spirits. Directory listings say it has been in business since 1993 and is owned by David Hollander.$about$ where id = '8f895259-9d33-412e-bfcb-9adc2605935b';  -- Saint Joseph Off Sale Liquor (Hollander's St. Joseph Liquor Shoppe)
update public.places set about = $about$St. Joseph Meat Market is a family-owned butcher shop that has sold fresh meat and homemade sausage downtown for generations. Al Pfannenstein bought it in 1968, his son Harvey ran it from 1997, and Harvey's daughter Wendy took over in 2025. The shop makes more than 150 kinds of sausage and 60 kinds of brats, its maple breakfast links won national Best of Show, and it does custom butchering and venison processing.$about$ where id = '8d32d5e6-2c7b-47d4-8b58-86afc63e6442';  -- St Joseph Meat Market Inc
update public.places set about = $about$Jupiter Moon is an artisan ice cream shop in downtown St. Joseph, with a seasonal second spot at Munsinger Gardens in St. Cloud. Its ice cream is handcrafted in small batches with local ingredients where possible, and the menu always includes vegan, nut-free and gluten-free friendly flavors. The shop makes its own waffle cones and serves flights for trying several flavors at once.$about$ where id = '63fd93ff-7254-461c-9e64-b7c9169a56ae';  -- Jupiter Moon Ice Cream - St. Joseph
update public.places set about = $about$The Newsleaders publish the St. Joseph Newsleader and the Sartell-St. Stephen Newsleader, community papers covering local news, schools, sports, obituaries and public notices. The St. Joseph paper has been printed since 1995, and both post stories daily at thenewsleaders.com.$about$ where id = 'b69f0ecb-e938-45a8-861b-87ce92a01710';  -- The Newsleaders
update public.places set about = $about$W|R Home Co. is a women's boutique and home decor shop in the old St. Joseph fire and police building on 1st Ave NW. Friends and real estate agents Shantel Waytashek and Kendra Harlander started it in 2018 as Weathered Revivals pop-up shops and opened the store in 2022. It carries clothing, jewelry, gifts, baby items and home goods, and the owners also offer design consultations and room makeovers.$about$ where id = '132e001b-e5b6-45fa-8db8-18ec28eb0c85';  -- W|R Home Co.
update public.places set about = $about$New Orleans-inspired Southern cooking with house-made specialties, a fresh revolving menu, and a relaxed, no-rush dining atmosphere.$about$ where id = '02280501-5d7d-4c2b-8a6b-2ec671ce9c7c';  -- Krewe Restaurant
update public.places set about = $about$The Local Blend is a coffee house in a historic downtown building, open since 2006 and run by Stacie Stone. Its kitchen and bakery make muffins, scones, soups and pizza with organic and local ingredients where it can, and the coffee is roasted by Muggsy's Beans. Local and traveling musicians play its stage on select nights, and it has won Best Coffeehouse in the St. Cloud Times readers' poll several times.$about$ where id = 'ed7a8833-6520-42b5-8eda-b11694731209';  -- The Local Blend
update public.places set about = $about$Minnesota Street Market is a community-owned food and art co-op in the historic 1899 Loso Building downtown, open since 2011. It sells local eggs, produce, meat, honey and syrup from area farmers, sustainably raised foods from small producers, and work by more than 40 local artists, writers and musicians. Anyone can shop, and members get extra benefits.$about$ where id = '7566738c-0349-4b9e-837b-f0c5ad5ed64e';  -- Minnesota Street Market, Food & Art Co-op
update public.places set about = $about$Sunny Mary Meadow is a cut flower farm on a sixth-generation family farm in Stearns County. It sells flower subscriptions and wedding and celebration flowers, and it hosts farm tours, classes, U-pick events and pick-and-pizza nights. It also has a self-serve farm stand and is used as a photography backdrop.$about$ where id = '448b008c-6c70-4591-b3e6-f094d6e41899';  -- Sunny Mary Meadow
update public.places set about = $about$The Middy is a small, casual bar on Minnesota Street downtown, known for drinks at a fair price and good conversation. It has pool tables and dartboards and draws both locals and college students.$about$ where id = 'ef33e2f0-a5e6-47da-b91f-23f2142adcd3';  -- The Middy
update public.places set about = $about$La Playette, known around town as The La, has been a St. Joseph neighborhood bar since Kay and Dirk Dierkhising opened it in 1958. It is a hangout for townies and CSB and SJU students alike, with pool tables, darts and live music.$about$ where id = '1f6263f8-77cb-4e9a-a767-c8326723e9c3';  -- La Playette Bar
update public.places set about = $about$KPower Yoga is a hot yoga studio with locations in St. Joseph, Sartell and Rogers, co-owned by Kelsey and Meghann. Its 45 to 60 minute classes start from power yoga and mix in strength training, cardio and pilates. The first class is free for newcomers.$about$ where id = 'e70d7fad-c801-48f5-b874-2191defaf9b5';  -- KPower Yoga
update public.places set about = $about$Milbert Johnson Family Dentistry provides comprehensive dental care for patients of all ages, offering services ranging from routine check-ups to advanced treatments. With a focus on comfort, patient education, and personalized care, the practice strives to help families maintain healthy, beautiful smiles in a welcoming and professional environment.$about$ where id = '1b35c7a9-713b-4da7-906e-4f74b0c2cb80';  -- Milbert Johnson Family Dentistry
update public.places set about = $about$Milk & Honey Ciders is a farmhouse cidery and orchard in the hills west of St. Joseph, started by childhood friends Peter Gillitzer, Adam Theis and Aaron Klocker. It makes dry, aromatic ciders from heirloom and traditional cider apples with minimal intervention, along with ice cider and pommeau. The taproom hosts a summer concert series, private events and weddings.$about$ where id = '796f4577-dd1a-49f6-aac5-49d3f8632ecb';  -- Milk & Honey Ciders
update public.places set about = $about$Neighbors Route 75 is an American bar and grill on County Road 75 that opened in 2018, one of three Neighbors restaurants owned by Joe Holtz. The kitchen makes its soups from scratch and hand-pats its burgers, using local produce where it can. The bar has 17 taps, some from local breweries, and a wall of TVs for watching games.$about$ where id = '3a51b1c2-eb45-4de4-8e38-5b48ca6ef44f';  -- Neighbors Route 75
update public.places set about = $about$Powerhouse Outdoor Equipment is a family-owned dealer on Cedar Street that sells and services outdoor power equipment, including mowers, trimmers, blowers and snow blowers. It carries brands such as Toro, STIHL, Exmark, Honda and Husqvarna and serves customers around St. Joseph and St. Cloud.$about$ where id = '48258ad2-2c0c-4d87-ab65-950e7ab083e4';  -- Powerhouse Outdoor Equipment
update public.places set about = $about$Sentry Bank began in 1904 as the First State Bank of St. Joseph, and it still has its main office in town on 4th Ave NE. It took the name Sentry Bank in 2011 as it grew into St. Cloud and St. Stephen. It offers personal and business checking, savings, loans and home mortgages.$about$ where id = 'fea5593e-15d0-446e-85b0-4bbc42dbda0c';  -- Sentry Bank
update public.places set about = $about$Solar Nails is a nail salon on County Road 75 offering manicures, pedicures and nail art. It is a popular spot for bridal parties and girls' days out as well as everyday self-care.$about$ where id = '2b59f99a-f6da-4c3a-86c3-a5b10b1ca8e3';  -- Solar Nails of St Joseph
update public.places set about = $about$The St. Joseph Farmers' Market is one of the oldest farmers markets in central Minnesota, held Friday afternoons from May to October at the Lake Wobegon Trailhead by Resurrection Lutheran Church. More than 30 farmers and artisans sell there, and most weeks bring music, kids' crafts or other entertainment. Kids and seniors get free market coupons funded by local businesses, and SNAP/EBT dollars are matched up to $10.$about$ where id = '4a213aca-4735-40dd-9ac4-2b58696a0427';  -- St. Joseph Farmers' Market
update public.places set about = $about$Two Bits is a one-man men's grooming salon downtown, where barber Brian has cut men's hair since 2000. Each client gets a one-on-one appointment for cuts, shaves, styling and beard trims, a classic barber cut that keeps up with modern styles.$about$ where id = 'bfcfe784-444a-44b5-835f-f3518032899c';  -- Two Bits Men's Grooming Salon
update public.places set about = $about$Direct primary care, urgent care, hormone health and a Medical Spa. WELL & Company offers personalized wellness in St. Joseph and Alexandria, MN.$about$ where id = '16b7e598-78b2-4b10-a95b-e03958879fe0';  -- WELL & Company St. Joseph
update public.places set about = $about$Wildwood Ranch is a family-run maple syrup operation inside Kraemer Lake-Wildwood County Park that has been tapping trees for more than 40 years. Each spring it opens its sugar shack for free public tours, showing both old wooden buckets and modern vacuum lines before the sap is boiled into syrup. Its syrup is sold at local spots including Minnesota Street Market.$about$ where id = 'b367e8ab-b872-4142-b814-ecdd4e318d5d';  -- Wildwood Ranch Maple Syrup
update public.places set about = $about$Whitby Gift Shop boasts a large variety of items for sale, many handmade by the sisters. You will find candles, tea towels, items for infants, cards for all occasions, jewelry, pottery, religious items, scarves, artwork, and much more. It sits in the Art and Heritage Place at Saint Benedict's Monastery, alongside the Haehn Museum.$about$ where id = 'bc27d1cb-ec01-4a70-a084-9948376f8a2a';  -- Whitby Gift Shop & Gallery
